# Technology Usage Documentation

When a session **adds or modifies** a technology in the stack, the agent MUST create or update its usage documentation in `docs/` **in the same session** by following the `document-feature` skill.

## Triggers

| Change type | Examples |
|---|---|
| New component added | Helm chart, operator subscription, script, integration |
| Version or image changed | Chart version bump, operator CSV update, image tag/digest change |
| Deploy path or prereqs changed | New Makefile target, values file restructure, new dependency |
| Verify / troubleshoot updated | New health check, validated error workaround |
| First cluster validation | Component deployed and confirmed working for the first time |

## Required action

1. Read the `document-feature` skill and follow its full checklist.
2. Create or update the primary guide (`docs/<component>-installation.md` or `docs/<component>/`).
3. Complete cross-links (README, AGENTS.md, ROADMAP).
4. Record validated versions and cite official sources per `documentation-sources` rule.

## Scope boundaries

| Concern | Handled by |
|---|---|
| Architecture decisions (add/swap/remove component) | `adr` skill + `adr-alignment` rule |
| CRD fields, operator channels, API endpoints | `documentation-sources` rule |
| Install/verify/troubleshoot procedures | **This rule** + `document-feature` skill |
| Index docs vs repo layout (README, AGENTS.md trees, ROADMAP links) | `docs-repo-alignment` rule + `sync-repo-docs` skill |

## Exceptions

- Typo-only or formatting-only fixes to existing docs
- Refactors that do not change external behavior, versions, or deploy steps
- Changes scoped entirely to ADR or doc files that are already aligned
